From 1696d701cda1e2eb9b6679c950235211119aaa27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 08:30:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add AltiVec decode kernels for PowerPC G4/G5

Five float-build decode kernels in celt/ppc/celt_altivec.c, hooked up through
celt/ppc/celt_altivec.h in the MIPS style: OVERRIDE_* macros that point the
existing celt/pitch.h and celt/mathops.h dispatch straight at the AltiVec
functions, with no run-time dispatch table.

  comb_filter_const        the 5-tap post-filter
  celt_deemphasis          mono contiguous de-emphasis
  deemphasis_stereo_simple stereo de-emphasis with interleaved output
  celt_float2int16         scale/clamp/round to int16
  celt_inner_prod          dot product

The whole file and all the overrides are behind
OPUS_PPC_PRESUME_ALTIVEC && !FIXED_POINT && big-endian, so every other
configuration compiles the file to nothing and is bit-identical to before.

Implementation notes:

- There is no VSX, so nothing may be loaded or stored unaligned.  Every
  kernel runs a scalar head until its store pointer is 16-byte aligned, then
  an aligned-store vector body, then a scalar tail, and reads through
  lvsl + two lvx + vperm.  The second load uses offset 15 rather than 16 so
  it can never reach a block past the last byte wanted.
- comb_filter_const keeps the five taps as five sliding windows into one
  chained load stream, as in the FFmpeg AltiVec post-filter.  The chain runs
  one block ahead, touching x[i-T+9]; the decoder calls this in place, and
  T >= COMBFILTER_MINPERIOD (15) keeps that read behind the store pointer.
- De-emphasis expands the IIR over four samples as a two-step scan,
  s1 = t + c*shift1(t), s = s1 + c^2*shift2(s1), with the incoming state
  folded into lane 0.  This re-associates the sum, so equivalence with C is
  by tolerance, not bit-exactness.  The VERY_SMALL bias is kept: it guards
  the G4's slow denormal path.
- The stereo kernel needs an 8-byte-aligned pcm pointer to be able to reach
  16-byte alignment by whole interleaved pairs; otherwise it stays scalar.
- float2int16 uses vec_round (vrfin), which rounds ties to even exactly like
  lrintf under the default rounding mode.

Under --enable-check-asm each kernel runs its C twin on a copy of the inputs
and asserts agreement: 1 LSB for int16, and for floats 1e-4 relative to the
loudest sample of the block rather than to the individual value, since the
re-association perturbs every output by about 1e-7 of the block's signal
level and an output landing on a zero crossing is arbitrarily smaller than
that.  The de-emphasis state is celt_sig-scale while its output is res-scale,
so its reference level is scaled by CELT_SIG_SCALE to match.  The comb filter
reference mirrors the caller's aliasing, because with y == x the filter is
deliberately self-referential from i = T-2 on.

